# Production build overrides. Values here win over .env, which carries whatever
# a developer's machine happens to need.
#
# This must be present and EMPTY, not absent. `src/lib/api.ts` treats an empty
# base as "decide per side": the server renders against loopback, the browser
# uses a relative path so it rides the nginx origin it was served from. A value
# inherited from .env is baked into the client bundle at build time, and a
# developer's 127.0.0.1 then becomes every visitor's browser calling their own
# machine — which is how the myth demo went down once already.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=
